#### Varying Data Centrality

A study was conducted on the effect of varying the centrality of AuAu 200 GeV collisions. This analysis used the same cuts as listed in Table 4.2, with the exception that \(\mid V_{z}\mid\leq\) 35 cm. The CSPM predicts that F(\(\xi\)) should decrease with increasing energy and increasing centrality.

The AE and EbE \(F(\xi)\) values do indeed appear to decrease with increasing centrality. The EbE \(F(\xi)\) is also always larger than the AE \(F(\xi)\). This is most likely due to the nature of the fit on an event by event basis with fewer statistics than the AE method. The expected temperature from both methods show a slight decrease in temperature with the transition to peripheral collisions.

